# Build-time API base for a DEPLOYED build that talks to the DEVELOPMENT backend.
# The Shell on app-dev.habify30.k-a-d-o.com (`npm run build:dev`) and the peer app on
# peer-dev.habify30.k-a-d-o.com (`npm run build:peer:dev`, DL-086 origin split).
#
# Development has no custom gateway domain — `api.habify30.k-a-d-o.com` is mapped to
# Production (DL-082 §1) — so this is the raw Catalyst Development URL, the same
# target the dev server proxies to in vite.config.ts.
#
# `npm run dev` does NOT read this file: there the browser calls `/api` same-origin
# through the Vite proxy, which is why VITE_API_BASE stays unset in dev.
#
# The mode is called `devbackend`, not `development`: `vite build --mode development`
# would also flip NODE_ENV and produce an unminified React development bundle. Any
# other mode name keeps the build in production mode and only swaps the .env file.
VITE_API_BASE=https://habify30-20116360871.development.catalystserverless.eu/server
